#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:502
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "whose it is"
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1370
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Only a process drawn in Potok that starts on a signal hears the groups above and below."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:454
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "hears groups above and below"
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:485
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "signal from groups around"
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:975
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A field the processes drawn in a group keep for each other: a step sets it, or adds a number to it, and every drawn process of the group reads it. It has a type, a text, a number, a yes or no, a date, a date and time, or one of its choices, and keeps a value of that type as a text. The group's editors declare it, or a drawing that sets it brings it along. A group has at most 50, each name once, and one a drawn process uses cannot be deleted. Deleting the group takes them along, and the process that wrote one last may go first."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1416
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A text, a number, a yes or no, a date, a date and time, or a choice."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1423
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Only a choice has choices, at most 30."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2157
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "What a process writes starts no other process: its messages and the sub-groups it makes set nothing going, so two processes never keep each other running by chance. A drawn process talks to another only by a step drawn for it. A call starts a drawn <AppProcess>process</AppProcess> that starts when another calls it, of the same group or a public one of a group above or below, and hands over what it takes; the <ValueProcess>run</ValueProcess> it starts is one level deeper, and in its own group it shares the caller's subject. A caller that waits goes on when that run ends, knowing which end it reached, or gives up at its deadline and cancels it. Cancelling a run cancels the run it waits for, and a run whose called run is cancelled stops, for an editor to take up again, which calls anew. A step can also keep a <GroupField>field of the group</GroupField>, which every drawn process of the group reads as its type; adding to one takes its lock, so two runs never lose each other's count, and a value not of its type is refused. A signal wakes the runs of the group's drawn processes that wait for it just then, at most 100, and starts the processes that start on it; nothing keeps it for a run that comes to wait later, and a wait may take only a signal sent on its own subject. A wait or a start that hears the groups above and below also takes their signals, as the entity it expects, and a run started so gets nothing of the sender's subject or people; a group beside never hears them. Runs go at most three processes deep, and a process another one of its group calls cannot be deleted."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:489
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "choices of a choice"
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:488
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "type of what it holds"
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2089
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A link to a form in a <Value>value</Value> gets a card with the form's own title and subtitle, read from its settings when the value is posted. The page asks for each reader whether they may open the form: its members may, and everyone may when the form takes non-members in a public <Group>group</Group>. The others see the card a guest would get, when the group is public, and otherwise only the link. A <GroupNotice>notice</GroupNotice> reaches followers nobody asks about, so it carries only a card anyone may see."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2087
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A link to a form shows its card to whoever may open it"
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:414
